# Go lineage 2 — initial ABI v1 handoff

## Submission

Initial service implementation, normal priority only, with four encoding slots
and baseline one-job admission/terminal WriteBatches. No ABI v2 implementation,
group commit, kernel replacement, Bitcoin library, external source, or evaluator
access. The supplied public smoke check is the only provided check used.

Deliverables: `build.sh`, Linux AArch64 `service`, Go/C source at workspace root,
the supplied storage helper plus `reuse/iterator.go`, Go tests,
`tests/integration.py`, `test.sh`, and `EXPERIMENTS.md`.

Build and test only through the pinned Linux broker:

```sh
python3 run.py './build.sh' 300
python3 run.py './test.sh' 300
```

Launch: `service DATADIR SOCKET_PATH`. The socket must be fresh. Send the wire
`shutdown` operation for a draining, zero-exit shutdown. A fresh invocation with
the same datadir recovers pending jobs and receipts. Build uses Go 1.27.1, cgo,
the supplied `/adapter/librosetta.so`, and dynamic `-lrocksdb`, with adapter rpath.
No downloads or third-party Go modules are needed.

Final executable SHA-256:
`9457f32f062ad0b86dfbef30c90b1f0c4be1e4cfff2c7eb6c3a18fc8c35e8817`.
ELF architecture, dynamic libraries, adapter RUNPATH, and v1-only verify symbol
